  "lang-tales-of-troy-1973": "subset: PG 1973 'Ulysses the Sacker of Cities' is one part of Tales of Troy and Greece (PG 32326 held)",
  "lang-selections": "selections from books already held: Ballades & Rhymes (PG 3138), The Magic Ring (PG 48032), Pretty Goldilocks, The Golden Mermaid, The Snow Man, Dick Whittington, Little Red Riding-Hood, Jack the Giant-Killer, Prince Darling, Twenty-two and Ten / XXII Ballades (early state of Ballades in Blue China), Iliad and Odyssey combined reissue, all modern reissues (Rainbow, Rose, Fifty Favorite... fairy books)",
  "lang-king-arthur-49057": "adaptation by J. C. Allen of The Book of Romance (PG 49057) — not Lang's text",
  "lang-fairy-books-index": "PG 30580 is David Widger's linked index to the fairy books, not a text",
  "lang-other-authors-edited": "other authors' works that Lang only edited, introduced or annotated: Scott's Waverley novels (PG 5998, 42389, 43678, 44247; IA 'Waverley novels' 1893-94), Dickens's Works (1897-98), Stevenson Swanston ed. (PG 21686 &c.), Perrault's Popular Tales (PG 33931), Kirk's Secret Commonwealth (PG 75485), Stoddart's Death-Wake (PG 16601), R. F. Murray's Poems (PG 1333), Gosse's Raleigh (PG 27580), Longinus tr. Havell (PG 17957), Dayrell's Folk Stories from Southern Nigeria (PG 34655), Parker's Euahlayi Tribe (PG 3819), van Eeden's Little Johannes (PG 40656), Nerval's Sylvie (PG 40492), Deulin's Johnny Nut (PG 47428), Dumas's My Memoirs (PG 49678), Murray's Hamewith (PG 51412), Hawthorne's Lock and Key Library (PG 2031), Burns's Poems and Songs, Herodotus Euterpe (Tudor tr.), Colonna's Strife of Love in a Dream, Thomas's Crystal Gazing, Social England Illustrated, Elizabethan Songs, Grimm's Household Tales (tr. Hunt, intro Lang — now held on the Grimm shelf, `grimm-hunt-1884-01`), Malory's Morte Darthur (ed. Sommer, essay by Lang), Molière's Précieuses ridicules — each belongs on its own author's shelf",
  "lang-multi-author": "multi-author volumes with a Lang chapter: Cricket (PG 52684), Anthropology and the Classics (PG 53646), The Progress of the Century (PG 55546), A Batch of Golfing Papers (1892), Poets' Country (1907), Presidential Addresses to the SPR, The Great Streets of the World",
